@model ReformedHistory.Views.Content.Confessions.Secret.SecretSection

<h2 id="@this.Model.Link">Chapter @this.Model.Index</h2>
<h3>@this.Model.Name</h3>
<br />

<div class="centerQuote">
    <span>
        Reprobation is not a decree necessarily excluding persons not-elect from all 
        possible means of salvation; but a decree permitting such out of freedom of their 
        own wills to neglect and abuse such means of their salvation.
    </span>
    <span>Bishop John Davenant, Animadversions</span>
</div>
    
<ol>
    <li>
        God created man in His own image with a most free will, not determined to conform to God's will but
        free to desire its own ends.
    </li>
    <li>
        God by no means hates any of his creatures, including those who freely reject Him. No person God 
        has created is barred from the means of grace, and all may come to faith, 
        believe in Christ, be baptized for the forgiveness of their sins, and be regenerated in the Holy Spirit.
    </li>
    <li>
        Nevertheless, those whom God did not predestine to be conformed to the image of His Son, known as the
        reprobate, will freely reject God, despise the Holy Spirit, fall into unbelief, and renounce the faith.
    </li>
</ol>
<br />